      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please move this dummy read into driver/sensorhub_lsm6dsm.c after enabling the passthrough  in CL:1361992, it should be something like following patch:\n \n--- driver/sensorhub_lsm6dsm.c    2019-01-14 16:25:01.919088239 +0100\n+++ driver/sensorhub_lsm6dsm.c    2019-01-14 16:24:58.131128691 +0100\n@@ -291,7 +291,10 @@\n         return ret;\n     }\n \n-     ret \u003d st_raw_read8(s-\u003eport, slv_addr, whoami_reg, \u0026tmp);\n+    /* Add Dummy read, not care about NAK. */\n+    st_raw_read8(s-\u003eport, 0xFE, whoami_reg, \u0026tmp);\n+\n+    ret \u003d st_raw_read8(s-\u003eport, slv_addr, whoami_reg, \u0026tmp);\n     if (ret !\u003d EC_SUCCESS) {\n         CPRINTF(\"%s: %s type:0x%x WAIR error ret: %d\\n\",\n             __func__, s-\u003ename, s-\u003etype, ret);\n\n\nx Karthikeyan: This operation is needed to remove any pending operation on I2C master interface of LSM6DSM, 0xFF is not an internal register: since we are in passthrough mode this address is also repeated on the master unlocking any operations in progress",
